{"agent_id":"pp3g-enJQ-adversarial-review-of-refined-suite-v2-hy4-preview","agent_seq":7,"timestamp":"2026-09-01T12:06:24.624996219Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"94ce32bc-7ebc-4768-af6a-4897cba03366","comment_uuid":"096e19b1-fe96-444d-9598-2e1602d3ae82","author":"pp3g-enJQ-adversarial-review-of-refined-suite-v2-hy4-preview","content":"[RESULT] Adversarial review of Observer Conformance Suite v2 — Hy4 Preview, complete.\n\nREVIEWED: feature/pp3g-feR2-synthesize-four-meta-reviews-into-refined-suite-v2 @65d9bb78 (suite 2038 lines; corpus 1754; committed baseline 282).\nROLE: Hy4 Preview, session pp3g-enJQ, agent type reviewer (read-only — see ARTIFACT NOTE at the end).\n\nVERDICT (derived by v2's own §33.2 algebra over MY reviewer statuses, not copied from §33.6): **REWORK**.\n- Rule 1 (FAIL): does not fire — no Critical obligation carries reviewer status FAILED. My only divergence from the builder is §3: VERIFIED → PARTIAL, not FAILED.\n- Rule 2 (BLOCKED): does not fire — no Critical obligation is BLOCKED.\n- Rule 3 (PASS): fails on every clause — ~20 Critical dimensions are not VERIFIED, §30 is OPEN (and my own review is not discharged, see below), §29 is SELF-ASSESSED with 3 of 14 items partial, the §31.1 mutation minimum is not executed.\n- Rule 4: REWORK. Converges with §33.6 — but note the convergence is weak evidence, because the algebra is under-specified (HY-2); both routes land on REWORK for the same dominant reason (20+ Critical dimensions unverified), not because the algebra is reliable.\n\nREVIEWER STATUS TABLE: 35 of 36 dimensions converge with the builder; 1 diverges (§3 Checklist Semantics VERIFIED → PARTIAL; counterexamples: §29's H2 heading uses the out-of-vocabulary token SELF-ASSESSMENT, and §38 row 33 carries '**REWORK**' outside §0.1's five-value vocabulary). Convergence is recorded as convergence, never assumed (§30.1).\n\nFINDINGS (severity per the suite's own §0.5.6 scale):\n- HIGH: HY-1 prose/table integrity (4 divergences); HY-2 algebra not total (obligation vs dimension vs row granularity, no projection defined); HY-3 criticality double-defined + I8 unclassified (escapes the mutation minimum); HY-4 two of four baselines still not in git, incl. the one §39's terms-of-art disposition rests on.\n- MEDIUM: HY-5 §39 machine cannot execute RF4 / unnamed unreachable terminal state / no expiry-during-review edge / no adjudication timeout / adjudicator not named; HY-6 §0.3 floor has no carrier and no retro-application (F4 survives); HY-7 §40.2 missing 4 corpus findings (Deepseek #11, Flash F7, Muse D4, Muse D5) + disposition arithmetic wrong; HY-8 PASS unreachable for I10 until its detector is executable.\n- LOW: HY-9 corpus hygiene (7th review delimited by a bare line; §0.4 points at the wrong section); HY-10 D9 unverified, Stop-Button sibling absent from git.\n\nATTACK LOG (29 logged attacks; 16 DEFEATED the suite, 12 HELD, 1 inconclusive) — target | expected-if-conforming | observed:\nHELD: (1) D19's own arithmetic — v1 prose 11 vs v1 table 23, confirmed accurate. (2) criticality tally 25/9/2 matches the stated claim. (3) §33.2 applied to the current table yields REWORK deterministically. (4) all 9 pinned baseline SHAs resolve. (5) T28–T33 absent (D1 accurate). (6) committed checklist structurally sound: 36 §§, 11 evidence classes, 4 verdicts, §23=7, §30=15. (7) checklist authenticity counter-fitting test: it contradicts the suite (§29 has 14 items vs the suite's \"thirteen\") — evidence it was not reconstructed to fit; provenance nonetheless unrecorded. (8) §40.2 attribution fidelity: all 34 citations I checked resolve to real, correctly-described source findings. (9) harness-run freshness: artefact @68750f28 is 2026-08-29, the run is 2026-08-30, no observer.sh change since — §0.5.4 not violated. (10) 36/36 dimension coverage preserved v1→v2. (11) all tables pipe-balanced; all §/D/I/F/RF/T/G cross-refs resolve. (12) §26.1 covers all five of Muse F1's counterexample classes.\nDEFEATED: §36 PARTIAL count (23 vs 24); §29 gate-item count (13 vs 14) and \"3 of 13\"; §38 row 33 REWORK cell; §29 heading SELF-ASSESSMENT (D10 half-fixed); §40.2 disposition arithmetic (21/7 vs 22/6); criticality defined twice; no obligation-level status register; §8 F11–F16 projection-dependent verdict (REWORK or FAIL from the same rows); §39 RF4 has no enabling edge; §39 terminal state unnamed/unreachable; no IN-REVIEW expiry edge; adjudicator named only as a role; VSDD.md + Adaptation Profile absent from git; §0.3 floor has no evidence carrier; §40.2 not exhaustive (4 untracked findings); I8 unclassified.\nINCONCLUSIVE: applying §0.5.5 (underclaiming) to §5/§8/§19/§21 — §0.1 has no status value for \"obligation unverifiable because the feature does not exist\", and BLOCKED's entry requirements (owner + acquisition attempt + escalation) are unmet for F11–F16, so by §0.1 those rows are invalid BLOCKED and revert to OPEN. Adjudication requested.\n\nFIVE ADJUDICATION REQUESTS (§33.4 — each is a dispute the algebra cannot resolve):\n1. Which criticality definition governs, §33.1's or §38's preamble?\n2. What is the row→dimension projection §33.2 consumes (max, any, or per-obligation)?\n3. Are barrier-absent forbidden transitions (F11–F16) FAILED under §0.1, or OPEN/BLOCKED? Ruling FAILED flips §8 (Critical) and therefore the verdict to FAIL.\n4. Is my §3 divergence (VERIFIED → PARTIAL) accepted?\n5. Name the adjudicator (§33.4 requires it named before the review runs; only a role is named today).\n\nWHAT SURVIVED ATTACK (credit where due — an uncalibrated review that is uniformly hostile is worthless):\n- Committing the canonical baseline (D18) was the highest-value change in v2 and paid for itself immediately: it is precisely what made the §29 miscount detectable. A defect made checkable is progress, not failure.\n- §33's algebra is a real improvement on v1: the verdict is derivable, the criticality column exists, and on this table it is robust (HELD).\n- §39's existence is right even where its transitions are incomplete; RF1–RF7 is a genuine forbidden-transition register for the review process.\n- §30.1–30.5 is a real asymmetry fix — and it bites: it forced this review to disclose its own non-discharge rather than claim completeness.\n- §40.2's attribution fidelity is high (34/34 spot-checked citations correct) — the gap is completeness, not honesty.\n- The appendix and §39.3 disclose the apparatus's central weakness in plain terms (\"there is no executable enforcement of a markdown document\"). The document does not oversell itself where it matters most.\n\nWHAT WOULD CHANGE MY VERDICT: a FAIL ruling on adjudication request 3. PASS remains unreachable until: I10 has an executable detector (HY-8), §30 is discharged by a review that attacks all 25 Critical dimensions, the mutation minimum is executed or its deferral formally accepted, and all Critical dimensions reach VERIFIED under a floored re-derivation.\n\nREPRODUCTION (the decisive checks; run against a checkout of the v2 branch):\n  git show feature/pp3g-feR2-synthesize-four-meta-reviews-into-refined-suite-v2:specifications/observer-conformance-suite.md > /tmp/v2.md\n  python3 - <<'PY'\n  import re\n  from collections import Counter\n  t=open('/tmp/v2.md',encoding='utf-8').read().splitlines()\n  # 1. summary-table tallies\n  st=[i for i,l in enumerate(t) if re.match(r'^## 38\\.',l)][0]\n  rows=[];seen=False\n  for l in t[st:]:\n      s=l.strip()\n      if s.startswith('|'): rows.append([c.strip() for c in s.strip('|').split('|')]);seen=True\n      elif seen: break\n  print('status tally', dict(Counter(r[3].split('(')[0].strip().upper() for r in rows[2:])))\n  print('crit tally  ', dict(Counter(r[4].split('(')[0].strip().title() for r in rows[2:])))\n  # 2. prose-vs-table\n  for i,l in enumerate(t,1):\n      for m in re.finditer(r'(\\d+|twenty-three|eleven|two)\\s+(?:dimensions\\s+)?(?:read|are|is)\\s+(PARTIAL|OPEN)',l):\n          print('prose claim line',i,repr(m.group(0)))\n  # 3. vocabulary\n  VOC={'OPEN','VERIFIED','PARTIAL','FAILED','BLOCKED'}\n  print('out-of-vocab rows',[(r[0],r[3]) for r in rows[2:] if r[3].split('(')[0].strip().upper() not in VOC])\n  # 4. baseline item counts in the committed checklist\n  c=open('/tmp/checklist.md',encoding='utf-8').read().splitlines()\n  for sec in (23,29,30):\n      i=[k for k,l in enumerate(c) if re.match(r'^## %d\\.'%sec,l)][0]\n      n=0\n      for l in c[i+1:]:\n          if re.match(r'^## \\d+\\.',l): break\n          if l.strip().startswith('[ ]'): n+=1\n      print('checklist section',sec,'items =',n)\n  PY\n(Full verifier — frontmatter, section contiguity, heading-vs-table drift, pipe balance, cross-ref resolution, row→dimension projection — was run for this review and is described check-by-check in my [REVIEW-HIGH] comment; it is not in git, see ARTIFACT NOTE.)\n\nWHAT-NOT-TESTED (this review's own negative space):\n1. I did not re-run the observer harness; all grading of implementation claims inherits v1's 2026-08-30 run (checked fresh against @68750f28, but not reproduced).\n2. I did not read observer.sh or run-tests.sh; every implementation claim in the suite is accepted as the builder's, not re-verified. My review is of the SUITE, not of the Observer.\n3. I did not attack each of the 25 Critical dimensions individually — §30.3's halting rule is NOT satisfied and this review is NOT §30.1-discharged; it cannot be consumed as the §30 gate result.\n4. No calibration corpus exists (v2 §30.4), so this review is uncalibrated: no seeded defects, no positive control, no measure of my own false-negative rate. HY-1's four findings may be a subset.\n5. I could not verify the canonical checklist's provenance (single-agent commit, no prior copy in git); three authenticity tests passed, none is conclusive.\n6. The §40.2 citations were checked for existence and headline fidelity, not for whether each cited finding's full argument is faithfully represented.\n7. Line numbers in the suite are pinned to @68750f28; I did not re-pin or re-verify any of them.\n\nARTIFACT NOTE (needs an operator decision): this session runs as the reviewer agent type — file writes and all git writes are blocked by project policy. The review therefore exists as these Crosslink comments (durable, hub-synced) and NOT as a file in git, and the verification script exists only in /tmp. The kickoff's rule that decision-gating artefacts must be in git is not satisfiable in this role. If a file artefact is required, a Builder must be commissioned to commit (a) this review as specifications/Observer Conformance Suite v2 - Adversarial Review (Hy4 Preview).md and (b) the verifier as scripts/verify-conformance-suite.py; I have logged an intervention to that effect. blocker=role-permission (not a task blocker — the review itself is complete).","created_at":"2026-09-01T12:06:24.618750936Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:jJIE6yuhcX/8IuWkNpZZAbuHlqBUwFuSxcK44O0j/F0","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnwoFwrL8eq3EMH5fNvbFC+ddnAm5MEmOAWT0XcLBq6EAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABACX2S12Jrhbz5IV17uvmkjIcy+q0lQBnQ6Meh0+UkCu9/CKriMQAji1tcok3M1juJUr4TqMsc5DU3NxIZthaVDg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:jJIE6yuhcX/8IuWkNpZZAbuHlqBUwFuSxcK44O0j/F0","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnwoFwrL8eq3EMH5fNvbFC+ddnAm5MEmOAWT0XcLBq6EAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJ/6RONM6Fjwr1wvbOivVpuGV/qNr07u8/10HOMKzlwoEXiMQd5KnvI9K721s41nWqMTEqwbht7QiC4+pi/AMw0="}
